// CONTACT QUALITY PROBE -- READ ONLY, NO RESET, NO HALT, NO WRITE.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS
// ---------------
// InitTarget duration is the only signal that separates good contact from
// marginal contact on a hand-held TC2030. VTref does not: it read 3.300V in
// every failure so far, including the two on 2026-08-09 that went on to
// produce "Failed to preserve target RAM" and a confused core.
//
// id_target.jlink cannot supply it. It connects as a generic CORTEX-M4 -- on
// purpose, because BSF6C53 has two SWD contact sets and naming the part on the
// DWM1001C's pads yields a device mismatch instead of an answer -- and
// InitTarget is an nRF52-specific device-script step that a generic CORTEX-M4
// connect never runs. So the contact check and the contact MEASUREMENT are two
// different sessions, and this is the second one.
//
// It names NRF52840_XXAA to get the device script, and does nothing else. Two
// FICR reads over the AHB-AP with the CPU still running, then out. Safe to
// point at a wedged board for the same reason id_target.jlink is.
si 1
speed 4000
device NRF52840_XXAA
connect
mem32 0x10000100, 1
exit
